{
 "fps": 30,
 "total": 17996,
 "xf": 18,
 "titleAfter": 5,
 "shots": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_01.jpg",
   "start": 0,
   "end": 478,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Two thousand two hundred years in the ground. And this bronze sword came out still sharp, still bright, barely touched by rust. For decades, people said the reason was a secret chemical coating, a lost technology.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s01.mp3",
     "dur": 14.856,
     "start": 10,
     "end": 456
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_02.jpg",
   "start": 460,
   "end": 842,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The story went that Qin craftsmen coated their weapons in chromium, a method the modern world only patented in the twentieth century. Proof of something nobody should have known.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s02.mp3",
     "dur": 11.664,
     "start": 470,
     "end": 820
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_03.jpg",
   "start": 824,
   "end": 1096,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Alien engineers? A vanished super-civilisation? Or just a very good story that nobody checked for forty years?",
     "file": "ep/audio/s03.mp3",
     "dur": 7.992,
     "start": 834,
     "end": 1074
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 4,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_04.jpg",
   "start": 1078,
   "end": 1469,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Tonight we run the case like a conservation lab. Sample intake. Microscope. Chemical analysis. Soil test. And a final report, where every claim gets a score.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s04.mp3",
     "dur": 11.952,
     "start": 1088,
     "end": 1447
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 5,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_05.jpg",
   "start": 1451,
   "end": 1710,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Facts first, theories labelled. Open the sample bag.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s05.mp3",
     "dur": 3.552,
     "start": 1461,
     "end": 1568
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 6,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "C",
   "ch": [
    "I \u00b7 INTAKE",
    "Sample Received",
    "LINTONG \u00b7 29 MARCH 1974"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_06.jpg",
   "start": 1692,
   "end": 2040,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chapter one. Sample intake. The date is the twenty-ninth of March, nineteen seventy-four. Farmland near Lintong, outside Xi'an, in a dry year.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s06.mp3",
     "dur": 10.512,
     "start": 1702,
     "end": 2018
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_07.jpg",
   "start": 2022,
   "end": 2371,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Farmers are digging a well. One of them, Yang Zhifa, with his brothers and a neighbour, hits something hard. Not rock. Fired clay, and then a clay head, staring up.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s07.mp3",
     "dur": 10.536,
     "start": 2032,
     "end": 2349
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 8,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_08.jpg",
   "start": 2353,
   "end": 2643,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "They had found the army of the first emperor of China, Qin Shi Huang, buried near his tomb in the late third century BCE.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s08.mp3",
     "dur": 8.568,
     "start": 2363,
     "end": 2621
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 9,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_09.jpg",
   "start": 2625,
   "end": 3012,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The largest pit is about two hundred thirty metres long and sixty-two wide. More than three thousand figures stand in it, and the four main pits lie roughly seven metres down.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s09.mp3",
     "dur": 11.808,
     "start": 2635,
     "end": 2990
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 10,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_10.jpg",
   "start": 2994,
   "end": 3316,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Every face is different, though they were built from moulds, with details added by hand. An industrial army, made like a modern production line.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s10.mp3",
     "dur": 9.648,
     "start": 3004,
     "end": 3294
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 11,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_11.jpg",
   "start": 3298,
   "end": 3626,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And the weapons. More than forty thousand bronze items have been recovered: swords, spears, halberds, crossbow triggers, and arrowheads in bundles.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s11.mp3",
     "dur": 9.84,
     "start": 3308,
     "end": 3604
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 12,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_12.jpg",
   "start": 3608,
   "end": 3840,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Most weapons were looted or rotted long ago. The ones that survived are the samples on our bench.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s12.mp3",
     "dur": 6.648,
     "start": 3618,
     "end": 3818
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 13,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_13.jpg",
   "start": 3822,
   "end": 4063,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "One sword in particular became famous. Bright, sharp, and in a condition that made people ask how.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s13.mp3",
     "dur": 6.96,
     "start": 3832,
     "end": 4041
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 14,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_14.jpg",
   "start": 4045,
   "end": 4279,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Intake complete. Question for the lab: why did these weapons survive when others turn to green crust?",
     "file": "ep/audio/s14.mp3",
     "dur": 6.72,
     "start": 4055,
     "end": 4257
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 15,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "C",
   "ch": [
    "II \u00b7 THE CLAIM",
    "A Forty Year Belief",
    "THE CHROMIUM LEGEND"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_15.jpg",
   "start": 4261,
   "end": 4411,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chapter two. The claim. Where did the chromium story come from?",
     "file": "ep/audio/s15.mp3",
     "dur": 3.912,
     "start": 4271,
     "end": 4389
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 16,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_16.jpg",
   "start": 4393,
   "end": 4698,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Analysis of some of the swords found chromium on the surface. A thin layer, a few micrometres thick, was reported on the blades.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s16.mp3",
     "dur": 9.096,
     "start": 4403,
     "end": 4676
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 17,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_17.jpg",
   "start": 4680,
   "end": 4987,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chromium resists corrosion. That is why modern steel and car parts are chrome plated. So the idea seemed to explain everything.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s17.mp3",
     "dur": 9.144,
     "start": 4690,
     "end": 4965
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 18,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "L",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_18.jpg",
   "start": 4969,
   "end": 5390,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Popular versions added that the Qin had used chromate treatment, a process people link to the nineteen thirties in Germany. I could not verify that patent claim, so we mark it as popular lore.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s18.mp3",
     "dur": 12.96,
     "start": 4979,
     "end": 5368
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 19,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_19.jpg",
   "start": 5372,
   "end": 5663,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And then the leap. If ancient China had chromate coating, who taught them? Cue the lost civilisation and the visitors from the sky.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s19.mp3",
     "dur": 8.616,
     "start": 5382,
     "end": 5641
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 20,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "M",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_20.jpg",
   "start": 5645,
   "end": 5919,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The claim spread because it is so easy to believe. A museum case, a shining blade, a number with the word chromium in it.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s20.mp3",
     "dur": 8.04,
     "start": 5655,
     "end": 5897
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 21,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_21.jpg",
   "start": 5901,
   "end": 6165,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "But a coating is a claim about intention. It says someone applied the chromium on purpose. Science can test that.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s21.mp3",
     "dur": 7.728,
     "start": 5911,
     "end": 6143
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 22,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_22.jpg",
   "start": 6147,
   "end": 6361,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "So in this lab, we do not ask whether chromium is there. We ask where, how much, and why.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s22.mp3",
     "dur": 6.048,
     "start": 6157,
     "end": 6339
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 23,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_23.jpg",
   "start": 6343,
   "end": 6480,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Question one logged. Next station: the microscope.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s23.mp3",
     "dur": 3.48,
     "start": 6353,
     "end": 6458
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 24,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "C",
   "ch": [
    "III \u00b7 MICROSCOPE",
    "Looking Closer",
    "UCL \u00b7 QIN MAUSOLEUM MUSEUM"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_24.jpg",
   "start": 6462,
   "end": 6830,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chapter three. The microscope. Researchers from University College London and the Emperor Qin Shihuang's Mausoleum Site Museum looked at the weapons themselves.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s24.mp3",
     "dur": 11.184,
     "start": 6472,
     "end": 6808
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 25,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_25.jpg",
   "start": 6812,
   "end": 7134,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "They studied hundreds of pieces. In total, four hundred sixty-four weapon parts were analysed, a very large sample for this kind of question.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s25.mp3",
     "dur": 9.648,
     "start": 6822,
     "end": 7112
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 26,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_26.jpg",
   "start": 7116,
   "end": 7416,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Under magnification, the surface of the metal is not the mirror we imagine. Corrosion exists. Some of it is thin, some patchy.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s26.mp3",
     "dur": 8.904,
     "start": 7126,
     "end": 7394
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 27,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_27.jpg",
   "start": 7398,
   "end": 7702,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And here is a clue. Many of these weapons had wooden or bamboo shafts, and the shafts were covered with lacquer, a black resin coating.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s27.mp3",
     "dur": 9.048,
     "start": 7408,
     "end": 7680
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 28,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_28.jpg",
   "start": 7684,
   "end": 7935,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Lacquer was a high-status material in Qin China. And it was part of the weapon wherever the blade met the handle.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s28.mp3",
     "dur": 7.272,
     "start": 7694,
     "end": 7913
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 29,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "X",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_29.jpg",
   "start": 7917,
   "end": 8135,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "So the team did something simple. They mapped where the chromium appeared on each weapon, part by part.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s29.mp3",
     "dur": 6.192,
     "start": 7927,
     "end": 8113
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 30,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_30.jpg",
   "start": 8117,
   "end": 8323,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The pattern is not random. Chromium was strongest where the metal had touched the lacquered wood.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s30.mp3",
     "dur": 5.784,
     "start": 8127,
     "end": 8301
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 31,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_31.jpg",
   "start": 8305,
   "end": 8551,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "A coating you apply on purpose goes everywhere. A smear you pick up from lacquer goes only where the lacquer was.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s31.mp3",
     "dur": 7.128,
     "start": 8315,
     "end": 8529
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 32,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "C",
   "ch": [
    "IV \u00b7 SPECTROMETER",
    "Reading The Elements",
    "SURFACE CHEMISTRY"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_32.jpg",
   "start": 8533,
   "end": 8750,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chapter four. The spectrometer. A machine that reads the elements on a surface, point by point.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s32.mp3",
     "dur": 6.144,
     "start": 8543,
     "end": 8728
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 33,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_33.jpg",
   "start": 8732,
   "end": 9039,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The result, in the numbers: chromium was found on fewer than ten percent of the weapons tested. Thirty-seven weapons, not the whole army.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s33.mp3",
     "dur": 9.144,
     "start": 8742,
     "end": 9017
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 34,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_34.jpg",
   "start": 9021,
   "end": 9268,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "If the Qin had chromium plated their weapons as a standard process, almost all should have shown it. They do not.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s34.mp3",
     "dur": 7.152,
     "start": 9031,
     "end": 9246
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 35,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_35.jpg",
   "start": 9250,
   "end": 9635,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The chromium also followed the type of artefact, not the state of preservation. Well-preserved swords without chromium exist. Corroded ones with chromium exist too.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s35.mp3",
     "dur": 11.736,
     "start": 9260,
     "end": 9613
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 36,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "D",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_36.jpg",
   "start": 9617,
   "end": 9842,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "If the chromium were the shield, the protected pieces would carry it. They do not. The link is missing.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s36.mp3",
     "dur": 6.408,
     "start": 9627,
     "end": 9820
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 37,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_37.jpg",
   "start": 9824,
   "end": 10000,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Then the team measured the lacquer itself. And the lacquer is rich in chromium.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s37.mp3",
     "dur": 4.8,
     "start": 9834,
     "end": 9978
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 38,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_38.jpg",
   "start": 9982,
   "end": 10378,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "A later study found Qin lacquer contains about zero point zero seven six micrograms of chromium per milligram, and the soil around about zero point zero six six.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s38.mp3",
     "dur": 12.12,
     "start": 9992,
     "end": 10356
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 39,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_39.jpg",
   "start": 10360,
   "end": 10582,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The lab's own conclusion in plain words: the lacquer is the unintended source of the chromium.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s39.mp3",
     "dur": 6.312,
     "start": 10370,
     "end": 10560
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 40,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "C",
   "ch": [
    "V \u00b7 REPLICATION",
    "Can It Be Made To Work?",
    "ACCELERATED AGEING"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_40.jpg",
   "start": 10564,
   "end": 10787,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chapter five. The replication. If chromate coating really protected bronze, you can test that.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s40.mp3",
     "dur": 6.36,
     "start": 10574,
     "end": 10765
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 41,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "X",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_41.jpg",
   "start": 10769,
   "end": 11028,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The team made bronze test pieces with modern chromate conversion coatings, and left others plain, as controls.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s41.mp3",
     "dur": 7.536,
     "start": 10779,
     "end": 11006
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 42,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "X",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_42.jpg",
   "start": 11010,
   "end": 11228,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Then they buried them in soils and aged them in accelerated conditions, to see which survive.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s42.mp3",
     "dur": 6.168,
     "start": 11020,
     "end": 11206
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 43,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "X",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_43.jpg",
   "start": 11210,
   "end": 11440,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The coating was not the star. The soil was. In the acidic soil, even the treated pieces corroded.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s43.mp3",
     "dur": 6.6,
     "start": 11220,
     "end": 11418
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 44,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "X",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_44.jpg",
   "start": 11422,
   "end": 11675,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "A piece left in low-pH, low-quality soil corroded no matter what it wore. Chemistry beats ornament.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s44.mp3",
     "dur": 7.344,
     "start": 11432,
     "end": 11653
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 45,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_45.jpg",
   "start": 11657,
   "end": 11923,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Meanwhile, alkaline fine-grained soil kept bronze in surprisingly good shape, even without a magic coating.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s45.mp3",
     "dur": 7.776,
     "start": 11667,
     "end": 11901
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 46,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_46.jpg",
   "start": 11905,
   "end": 12226,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And the claimed coating was ten to fifteen micrometres thick. That is thinner than a human hair, far thinner than anyone could verify by eye.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s46.mp3",
     "dur": 9.624,
     "start": 11915,
     "end": 12204
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 47,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_47.jpg",
   "start": 12208,
   "end": 12385,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The replication did not support an ancient chrome coating as the preservative.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s47.mp3",
     "dur": 4.824,
     "start": 12218,
     "end": 12363
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 48,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "C",
   "ch": [
    "VI \u00b7 SOIL TEST",
    "The Real Preservative",
    "PH AND PARTICLE SIZE"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_48.jpg",
   "start": 12367,
   "end": 12529,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chapter six. The soil test. So why did so many weapons survive?",
     "file": "ep/audio/s48.mp3",
     "dur": 4.32,
     "start": 12377,
     "end": 12507
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 49,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_49.jpg",
   "start": 12511,
   "end": 12775,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The Qin pits were filled with very fine soil, packed tightly. Fine particles keep air and water moving slowly.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s49.mp3",
     "dur": 7.728,
     "start": 12521,
     "end": 12753
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 50,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_50.jpg",
   "start": 12757,
   "end": 13013,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The soil was also moderately alkaline. Alkaline conditions slow the corrosion of copper-tin bronze.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s50.mp3",
     "dur": 7.464,
     "start": 12767,
     "end": 12991
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 51,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_51.jpg",
   "start": 12995,
   "end": 13323,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The bronze itself was a high-quality copper and tin alloy, with traces of nickel, magnesium and cobalt, and it was cast with real control.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s51.mp3",
     "dur": 9.864,
     "start": 13005,
     "end": 13301
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 52,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_52.jpg",
   "start": 13305,
   "end": 13557,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The pits were built as sealed halls: wooden roofs, mats and packed earth, made to protect the army in the afterlife.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s52.mp3",
     "dur": 7.32,
     "start": 13315,
     "end": 13535
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 53,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_53.jpg",
   "start": 13539,
   "end": 13849,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The same roofs later burned and fell, as armies and looters came. Fire, collapse and decay are why many figures were found in pieces.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s53.mp3",
     "dur": 9.24,
     "start": 13549,
     "end": 13827
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 54,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_54.jpg",
   "start": 13831,
   "end": 14074,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "What survived intact did so by geography, luck and clean soil chemistry. No visitors required.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s54.mp3",
     "dur": 7.008,
     "start": 13841,
     "end": 14052
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 55,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_55.jpg",
   "start": 14056,
   "end": 14202,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Soil test complete. The environment preserved the weapons.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s55.mp3",
     "dur": 3.792,
     "start": 14066,
     "end": 14180
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 56,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "C",
   "ch": [
    "VII \u00b7 THE CRAFT",
    "An Industrial Army",
    "STATE PRODUCTION"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_56.jpg",
   "start": 14184,
   "end": 14435,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chapter seven. The craft. If there is no secret chemical, what is left? Something more impressive: organisation.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s56.mp3",
     "dur": 7.272,
     "start": 14194,
     "end": 14413
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 57,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_57.jpg",
   "start": 14417,
   "end": 14740,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Arrowheads were made in standardised batches. The chemistry of bundles of about a hundred points matches closely, a sign of batch production.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s57.mp3",
     "dur": 9.672,
     "start": 14427,
     "end": 14718
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 58,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_58.jpg",
   "start": 14722,
   "end": 15042,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The paint tells the same story. Cinnabar red, malachite green, azurite blue, and Han purple, a synthetic pigment, were all in use.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s58.mp3",
     "dur": 9.576,
     "start": 14732,
     "end": 15020
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 59,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_59.jpg",
   "start": 15024,
   "end": 15276,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Han purple is barium copper silicate, a manufactured pigment. Real chemistry. Not alien chemistry.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s59.mp3",
     "dur": 7.32,
     "start": 15034,
     "end": 15254
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 60,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_60.jpg",
   "start": 15258,
   "end": 15626,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And when the paint was first exposed to Xi'an's dry air, the lacquer underneath curled in about fifteen seconds and flaked within minutes. Fragile, brilliant, gone.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s60.mp3",
     "dur": 11.184,
     "start": 15268,
     "end": 15604
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 61,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_61.jpg",
   "start": 15608,
   "end": 15846,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The real wonder is a state that could mould, fire, paint and arm thousands of soldiers to a standard.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s61.mp3",
     "dur": 6.864,
     "start": 15618,
     "end": 15824
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 62,
   "fx": "score",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": [
    "LAB REPORT",
    "The Scorecard",
    "EVIDENCE VS THEORY"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_62.jpg",
   "start": 15828,
   "end": 15950,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Lab report. Time to score the chromium claim.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s62.mp3",
     "dur": 2.976,
     "start": 15838,
     "end": 15928
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 63,
   "fx": "score",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_63.jpg",
   "start": 15932,
   "end": 16292,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Chromium exists on some weapons: evidence. A deliberate protective coating: debunked. Chromium on over ninety percent of weapons: false, under ten percent had it.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s63.mp3",
     "dur": 10.92,
     "start": 15942,
     "end": 16270
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 64,
   "fx": "score",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_64.jpg",
   "start": 16274,
   "end": 16644,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Lacquer as the chromium source: strong evidence. Soil chemistry as the preservative: evidence. Lost technology or alien help: no evidence at all.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s64.mp3",
     "dur": 11.256,
     "start": 16284,
     "end": 16622
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 65,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_65.jpg",
   "start": 16626,
   "end": 16919,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The verdict. The chromium was real, but the coating was a myth. It was contamination from lacquer, and the real hero was the soil.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s65.mp3",
     "dur": 8.688,
     "start": 16636,
     "end": 16897
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 66,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_66.jpg",
   "start": 16901,
   "end": 17283,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The correction came from a joint team including the museum itself, published in Scientific Reports in twenty nineteen. Science corrected a forty-year belief in public.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s66.mp3",
     "dur": 11.664,
     "start": 16911,
     "end": 17261
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 67,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_67.jpg",
   "start": 17265,
   "end": 17685,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Next case: sixty-two schoolchildren in Zimbabwe in nineteen ninety-four, and what they said came down onto their playground. The story is very different, and the evidence is not a lab report.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s67.mp3",
     "dur": 12.912,
     "start": 17275,
     "end": 17663
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 68,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_68.jpg",
   "start": 17667,
   "end": 17921,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Did you believe the chrome story? Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery put to the test.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s68.mp3",
     "dur": 7.392,
     "start": 17677,
     "end": 17899
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}